commit 29550b6a9cef0657e6daa6353e8ef6edb6c90376
Author: ehsanmok <ehsanmok@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 16 03:18:32 2026 +0000

    fix(runtime): register shared listeners with EPOLLEXCLUSIVE without EPOLLRDHUP
    
    `Reactor.register_exclusive` combined `_interest_to_epoll(interest)` with
    EPOLLEXCLUSIVE. For read interest that mask is EPOLLIN | EPOLLRDHUP, and
    epoll_ctl(2) does not allow EPOLLRDHUP together with EPOLLEXCLUSIVE, so the
    call always failed with EINVAL. The kernel-<4.5 fallback then registered the
    listener plainly, and shared-listener workers all woke for every connection
    instead of using exclusive wakeups.
    
    The exclusive registration now clears EPOLLRDHUP, which a listener never
    needs. The fallback stays for kernels that really lack the flag, and its
    comment says that reaching it on a modern kernel is a bug.
    
    Exclusive wakeups go to one waiting worker per event rather than balancing
    connections, so with the fix a lightly loaded server can keep landing new
    connections on one worker (the reporter measured this). That is documented on
    `register_exclusive` and in the `HttpServer.serve` note on
    FLARE_REUSEPORT_WORKERS=0; rebalancing the listener is left as a follow-up.
    
    New tests in test_reactor read the mask back from /proc/self/fdinfo/<epfd>:
    register_exclusive must store EPOLLEXCLUSIVE and EPOLLIN without EPOLLRDHUP
    (it stored a plain registration before), and a plain register keeps
    EPOLLRDHUP so EVENT_HUP still works. Every shared-listener loop goes through
    this one method, so none needed a change. tests/_agg regenerated.
    
    Fixes #36
    
    Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

